task: one-binary-story
agent: opus-dataflow
started: 2026-09-12
branch: feature/one-binary-story
worktree: ../okay-wt-obs

why: the BACKLOG lane under "dataflow — direction": the small-business
  path told ONCE, as a worked example and not a module. The repository
  has a log, a windowed engine, a page, and a way to copy bytes off the
  machine, and nobody has run them end to end in one process. Until
  that runs in a test the "one binary" claim is a sentence.

what: one test (and one documentation section) that, in ONE process:
  events into an okay-persist log -> a windowed report over the log
  (Cluster.run over Streams.chunks, the stage 11 road) -> a page that
  renders the report -> a backup of the log written OUTSIDE the
  process's own directory and restored into a fresh store that answers
  the same report. Every step is a module the repository already has;
  the work is the seam between them and the one file that shows it.

what this is NOT: a new module, a server, or a deployment. If a seam
  is missing (say, the store has no backup road) that is the finding
  and it gets its own small lane, not a workaround inside the story.
